From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps5cemu <ps5cemu@localhost>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:16:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PS5: GetTickCount on the TSC, which the port turns on

clock_gettime is a call into the PS5's kernel, about 890 ns a call on a
console, and Cemu's GPU thread takes its millisecond clock at every draw
call (LatteCommandProcessor, for its texture cache's ages). Breath of the
Wild draws about 4,300 times a frame, so the clock took 3.3 ms of each
16.7 ms frame from the GPU thread; on the TSC it takes 11 ns a call. An
A/B on a console (2026-10-03) gave the GPU thread that time back. The
port turns it on before Cemu starts (PS5Cemu_UseTscTickCount), and can
leave it on clock_gettime.
---
 src/Common/unix/platform.cpp | 25 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/Common/unix/platform.cpp b/src/Common/unix/platform.cpp
index 879ae4d..9462c65 100644
--- a/src/Common/unix/platform.cpp
+++ b/src/Common/unix/platform.cpp
@@ -1,8 +1,33 @@
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <ctime>
 
+#if defined(CEMU_PS5)
+#include <x86intrin.h>
+extern "C" uint64_t sceKernelGetTscFrequency();
+
+// PS5: GetTickCount on the TSC, which the port turns on before Cemu starts (PS5Cemu_UseTscTickCount;
+// tscTickCount in ps5cemu.json). clock_gettime is a call into the console's kernel (about 890 ns a
+// call, measured), and the GPU thread takes the time at every draw call (LatteCommandProcessor, for
+// its texture cache's ages, in milliseconds): Breath of the Wild's 4,300 draws a frame cost its GPU
+// thread 3.3 ms of each 16.7 ms frame, which the TSC gave back (A/B on a console, 2026-10-03).
+static bool s_tscTickCount = false;
+static uint64_t s_tscPerMillisecond = 1;
+
+void PS5Cemu_UseTscTickCount(bool enabled)
+{
+	const uint64_t frequency = sceKernelGetTscFrequency();
+	s_tscTickCount = enabled && frequency >= 1000;
+	if (s_tscTickCount)
+		s_tscPerMillisecond = frequency / 1000;
+}
+#endif
+
 uint32_t GetTickCount()
 {
+#if defined(CEMU_PS5)
+	if (s_tscTickCount)
+		return (uint32_t)(__rdtsc() / s_tscPerMillisecond);
+#endif
 #if BOOST_OS_LINUX
 	struct timespec ts;
 	clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC_RAW, &ts);
